Z||000009||artherd||11-11-2001||09:04 PM||||My first thought was "You haven't heard a Ferrari in person, have you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">"<P>They can't be recorded.<P>Oddly enough, the Firebird in that video sounds similar to the 180crank, dry-sump V8 Ferraris...<P>Could it have a 180degree crankshaft? (George, I assume that's what you meant, or are you talking about a different exhaust heander configuration on a standard 90-degree crank V8 motor?)<P>Lotus V8s and Ferraris V8s are the only road cars I know of to come this way (the Masser too?) God they're great!<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>sounds good. But there is still no sound like a wound out Ferrari. Its music.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
